  "sessions": [],
  "quotes": [
    {
      "quote": "the models are so good that you can just keep the harness simple.",
      "timestamp_sec": 1,
      "talk_slug": "what-if-the-harness-mattered-more-than-the-model",
      "deep_link": "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=2e9ANoOEn28&t=1s",
      "speaker_attributed": true
    },
    {
      "quote": "that's moving in the wrong direction because that is making us reliant on fancy proprietary models that can't be run locally",
      "timestamp_sec": 52,
      "talk_slug": "what-if-the-harness-mattered-more-than-the-model",
      "deep_link": "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=2e9ANoOEn28&t=52s",
      "speaker_attributed": true
    },
    {
      "quote": "What if we focused on open-source models that can be run locally? What if we focused on building a harness that is so good that we can get the performance of a cutting-edge model through a local open-source model?",
      "timestamp_sec": 52,
      "talk_slug": "what-if-the-harness-mattered-more-than-the-model",
      "deep_link": "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=2e9ANoOEn28&t=52s",
      "speaker_attributed": true
    },
    {
      "quote": "So, scores range from 52.4% to 76.2%. So, more than a 20-point difference, and only the harness changed.",
      "timestamp_sec": 143,
      "talk_slug": "what-if-the-harness-mattered-more-than-the-model",
      "deep_link": "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=2e9ANoOEn28&t=143s",
      "speaker_attributed": true
    },
    {
      "quote": "the really interesting thing is that for weaker models, the harness matters more",
      "timestamp_sec": 143,
      "talk_slug": "what-if-the-harness-mattered-more-than-the-model",
      "deep_link": "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=2e9ANoOEn28&t=143s",
      "speaker_attributed": true
    },
    {
      "quote": "if a good harness can compensate, and can make a weaker model perform better, then you can build our own harnesses, and that's something that any of us can do, and we don't have to depend on paid models.",
      "timestamp_sec": 143,
      "talk_slug": "what-if-the-harness-mattered-more-than-the-model",
      "deep_link": "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=2e9ANoOEn28&t=143s",
      "speaker_attributed": true
    },
    {
      "quote": "I think building a good harness actually requires language-level support.",
      "timestamp_sec": 192,
      "talk_slug": "what-if-the-harness-mattered-more-than-the-model",
      "deep_link": "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=2e9ANoOEn28&t=192s",
      "speaker_attributed": true
    },
    {
      "quote": "how do you give agent capabilities so they can take actions, but not so much capability that they do something unsafe",
      "timestamp_sec": 386,
      "talk_slug": "what-if-the-harness-mattered-more-than-the-model",
      "deep_link": "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=2e9ANoOEn28&t=386s",
      "speaker_attributed": true
    },
    {
      "quote": "giving the agent the ability to read and write arbitrary files on our file system is really unsafe. So, by default Agency won't allow you to do this.",
      "timestamp_sec": 699,
      "talk_slug": "what-if-the-harness-mattered-more-than-the-model",
      "deep_link": "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=2e9ANoOEn28&t=699s",
      "speaker_attributed": true
    },
    {
      "quote": "here's the safe version of our agent where the tools will raise an interrupt by default, and now this code is going to ask the user, do you approve?",
      "timestamp_sec": 866,
      "talk_slug": "what-if-the-harness-mattered-more-than-the-model",
      "deep_link": "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=2e9ANoOEn28&t=866s",
      "speaker_attributed": true
    },
    {
      "quote": "And this is better, and it is safe, but it's also very slow. So, the next thing we want to do is make the agent autonomous, while still keeping it safe, and that's the tricky part",
      "timestamp_sec": 866,
      "talk_slug": "what-if-the-harness-mattered-more-than-the-model",
      "deep_link": "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=2e9ANoOEn28&t=866s",
      "speaker_attributed": true
    },
    {
      "quote": "we're locking the directory argument to demo. Um the LLM isn't going to be able to change that argument. It's not even going to know that that argument exists.",
      "timestamp_sec": 973,
      "talk_slug": "what-if-the-harness-mattered-more-than-the-model",
      "deep_link": "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=2e9ANoOEn28&t=973s",
      "speaker_attributed": true
    },
    {
      "quote": "partial function application is a really great way to constrain the capabilities of your agent. Now, no human input is needed, but it's still safe.",
      "timestamp_sec": 1014,
      "talk_slug": "what-if-the-harness-mattered-more-than-the-model",
      "deep_link": "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=2e9ANoOEn28&t=1014s",
      "speaker_attributed": true
    },
    {
      "quote": "in agency, a sub-agent is just another function. And you just call it, use it like a tool just like you would anywhere else.",
      "timestamp_sec": 1333,
      "talk_slug": "what-if-the-harness-mattered-more-than-the-model",
      "deep_link": "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=2e9ANoOEn28&t=1333s",
      "speaker_attributed": true
    },
    {
      "quote": "sub agents are cool because they let you add new capabilities without bloating context",
      "timestamp_sec": 1426,
      "talk_slug": "what-if-the-harness-mattered-more-than-the-model",
      "deep_link": "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=2e9ANoOEn28&t=1426s",
      "speaker_attributed": true
    },
    {
      "quote": "Often when agents get confused and fail, it's because they have too much context blow, but also because they have too many unrelated concepts in their context.",
      "timestamp_sec": 1485,
      "talk_slug": "what-if-the-harness-mattered-more-than-the-model",
      "deep_link": "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=2e9ANoOEn28&t=1485s",
      "speaker_attributed": true
    },
    {
      "quote": "So the baseline objective is 0.2 and it's going to try to improve upon that.",
      "timestamp_sec": 1580,
      "talk_slug": "what-if-the-harness-mattered-more-than-the-model",
      "deep_link": "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=2e9ANoOEn28&t=1580s",
      "speaker_attributed": true
    },
    {
      "quote": "the reason this self-optimization is so great is because we're not guessing and checking. We're systematically measuring and improving, which is a big leap forward.",
      "timestamp_sec": 1650,
      "talk_slug": "what-if-the-harness-mattered-more-than-the-model",
      "deep_link": "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=2e9ANoOEn28&t=1650s",
      "speaker_attributed": true
    },
    {
      "quote": "one of the really killer features of Agency is that when you raise that interrupt, it's actually going to pause execution and return control back to the user.",
      "timestamp_sec": 1797,
      "talk_slug": "what-if-the-harness-mattered-more-than-the-model",
      "deep_link": "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=2e9ANoOEn28&t=1797s",
      "speaker_attributed": true
    },
    {
      "quote": "You can serialize the execution, you can come back to it a week later, and you don't need to change anything about all the code we have been looking at.",
      "timestamp_sec": 1839,
      "talk_slug": "what-if-the-harness-mattered-more-than-the-model",
      "deep_link": "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=2e9ANoOEn28&t=1839s",
      "speaker_attributed": true
    },
    {
      "quote": "an agent is a model plus a harness for this talk, at least. Uh, better harness equals better performance, especially for weaker models.",
      "timestamp_sec": 1880,
      "talk_slug": "what-if-the-harness-mattered-more-than-the-model",
      "deep_link": "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=2e9ANoOEn28&t=1880s",
